1
00:00:03,222 --> 00:00:09,051
Group metered usage by Model and category to see which feature made the requests.

2
00:00:09,051 --> 00:00:15,483
Chat sessions, chat interactions, text messages, voice calls, the API, workflows and other

3
00:00:15,483 --> 00:00:17,962
agents each get their own rows.

4
00:00:18,427 --> 00:00:22,213
Model and purpose shows why the requests were made:

5
00:00:22,213 --> 00:00:27,925
to answer, to search, to index documents, to transcribe, to summarize, and more.

6
00:00:27,925 --> 00:00:31,047
Services that you add can name their own.

7
00:00:31,506 --> 00:00:35,976
Group completions by AI profile to see which assistant used the tokens, and

8
00:00:35,976 --> 00:00:37,962
how many chat sessions it had.

9
00:00:37,962 --> 00:00:41,770
That is the table to read when you want to know which assistant

10
00:00:41,770 --> 00:00:43,316
is the most expensive.

11
00:00:43,986 --> 00:00:48,668
Or group them by connection, to see which AI service account was used.

12
00:00:48,668 --> 00:00:52,981
A connection holds the address and the key of an AI service, and

13
00:00:52,981 --> 00:00:55,260
several profiles can share one.

14
00:00:55,260 --> 00:00:59,326
The other choices are user and model, model, and deployment.

15
00:01:01,118 --> 00:01:07,407
Voice calls can be grouped by deployment, AI profile, campaign, channel, engine or

16
00:01:07,407 --> 00:01:11,338
day, and audio usage by model, voice or language.

